{
  "tema": 6060,
  "slug": "ese-esa-eso-pronombre",
  "titulo": "Ese, esa, esos, esas, eso: that one, those",
  "subtitulo": "¿Ese? No, eso no.",
  "foto": "t06.jpg",
  "regla": "For that one / those (ones), use ese, esa, esos, esas, matching the noun. Eso (neutral, no plural) is for an unknown thing, an idea or something just said: Eso es mentira.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Ese** points to something a bit away from you, often near the person you're talking to: _that one_, _those ones_. No noun follows."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "",
            "Masculine",
            "Feminine",
            "Neutral"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "Singular",
              "**ese**",
              "**esa**",
              "**eso**"
            ],
            [
              "Plural",
              "**esos**",
              "**esas**",
              "—"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Match the gender and number of the thing: el carro → **ese**; las chanclas → **esas**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Eso** is neutral: for something you can't name, an idea, or what someone just said: ¿Qué es **eso**? **Eso** es mentira."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Everyday phrases: **¡Eso!** (_That's it! / Way to go!_), **por eso** (_that's why_), **eso sí** (_that's for sure_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Written **without an accent** today: **ese**, not _ése_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **eso** is _that thing_ or _that idea_. If you can't point at a noun, it's **eso**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "¿Cuál es tu carro? —==Ese==, el rojo.",
              "en": "Which one is your car? —That one, the red one."
            },
            {
              "es": "No me gustan estas papas; prefiero ==esas==.",
              "en": "I don't like these fries; I prefer those."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Qué es ==eso== que traes en la mano?",
              "en": "What's that you've got in your hand?"
            },
            {
              "es": "==Eso== que dijiste no es cierto.",
              "en": "What you said isn't true."
            },
            {
              "es": "Me dormí tarde; por ==eso== no fui a entrenar.",
              "en": "I went to sleep late; that's why I didn't go to training."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ves esas olas? ==Esas== son las buenas.",
              "en": "See those waves? Those are the good ones."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Esos== son los vecinos que tienen huerto en la azotea.",
              "en": "Those are the neighbors with the rooftop garden."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Eso==! Ya te salió la llave.",
              "en": "That's it! You nailed the submission."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
